==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|up shit creek without a paddle}}, {{l|en|up shit's creek}}, {{l|en|up shit's creek without a paddle}}

===Adjective===
{{head|en|adjective|head=[[up]] [[shit]] [[creek]]}}

# {{label|en|idiomatic}} In [[trouble]]; in a [[difficult]] situation.

====Usage notes====
* The addition of "without a paddle" in alternative forms is considered by some to suggest an [[intensification]] of the difficulty of the situation.
* Australian variant: "up shit creek in a barbed wire canoe with a rusty teaspoon for a paddle". Fairly typical example of applying hyperbole to freshen up a much used expression.

